# Phase 1 corpus derivation pipeline (F2/F8 fixes): eval-corpus/{source,db,md}/ hold UNSCRUBBED
# intermediates (raw sampled .db files and their md-tree exports) — these must never be committed.
# The generic `*.db`/`*.db-shm`/`*.db-wal` globs above already guard the .db files incidentally,
# but eval-corpus/md/ (pre-scrub markdown, containing the same emails/paths/keys the scrub step
# exists to remove) had no guard at all. Explicit paths here make the intent unambiguous rather
# than relying on an unrelated generic glob to happen to cover it.
eval-corpus/source/
eval-corpus/db/
eval-corpus/md/

# F8 fix: eval-corpus/publish/ (scrubbed, publishable) and its scrub-integrity marker are DERIVED
# artifacts, regenerated on demand via the 3-command pipeline (see eval-corpus/README.md) and
# delivered to the runner repo as run artifacts — not committed to source control. Kept on disk
# locally; just no longer tracked in git.
eval-corpus/publish/
eval-corpus/SCRUB_MANIFEST.json
